From: SP11 Linux audio parity project
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: implement SP11 Windows pull pipeline

The recovered Windows QGPR transaction, Qualcomm AudioReach/GSL sources and
REV_0D ACDB agree that the SP11 render source is SH_MEM_PULL_MODE, not the
WR_SHARED_MEM_EP endpoint substituted by the earlier Linux candidate.

Keep IID 0x4660 as MID 0x07001006 and implement its actual contract.
Map a dedicated position page and configure the mapped circular ring.
Register its watermark and soft-pause events. Send the exact pull/PCM/MFC
formats and use the DSP-updated position structure for ALSA progress. Do
not issue legacy per-period write-buffer commands for this graph.

Complete the captured pre-start sequence with the SP/SPVI GETs. Add the
volume gain, volume-step MSIIR, mute and channel-mixer stages. Send protected
graph commands through the graph client port and start the three subgraphs
in the captured root, speaker, render order. Retain the GSL-compatible policy
for unsupported graph calibration records, while failing closed on every
other required transaction.

This cumulative patch is based on the deployed audio-v2 source state and
supersedes the diagnostic-only endpoint experiments in patches 0010-0014.

